    30149,  ""
    30150,  "Debug level"
    30151,  "0 = TRACE, 1 = INFO, 2 = WARNINGS, 3 = ERRORS"
    30152,  "Error display mode"
    30153,  "This property let you choose the mode use to report errors.
- Annotation: make errors display inline. Use Annotations style option below to customize the annotations style.
- Dialog: make the error display in a scrollable dialog. All errors are display in a single dialog.
- Alert: display error in a single alert dialog."
    30154,  "Annotations style"
    30155,  "Error messages style when displayed as annotations.
Use ""Annotation preview"" button below to display an annotation sample."
    30156,  "Highlighted annotations style"
    30157,  "Highlighted error messages style when displayed as annotations.
Use ""Annotation preview"" button below to display an annotation sample."
    30158,  "Max displayed errors"
    30159,  "Maximum number of displayed errors. You can allow an infinite number of errors by setting the value `-1`, but be aware that it can slow down the application when XML has many errors."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    30160,  "Add node position in XPath"
    30161,  "Additionally shows the nodes position in XPath. When enabled, the XPath of ""<a><b></b><b>Content</b></a>"" will resolve to ""/a/b[2]"" instead of ""/a/b""."
    30162,  "Display current XPath in statusbar"
    30163,  "When enabled, current XPath is automatically printed in statusbar"
    30164,  "Identity attribute names"
    30165,  "Specifies a semi-colon separated list of attributes names which could contain identity values. The values of theses attributes are copied into statusbar xpath value. For instance, if attribute ""id"" is referenced and a tag ""<sample id='hello'>"" is present, the status bar will contain "".../sample[id='hello']/...""."
    30166,  "Dump attributes name"
    30167,  "Introduce the indentity attributes with their name. When enabled, elements are dumped like "".../sample[id='hello']/..."". When disabled, elements are dumped like "".../sample[hello]/...""."
    30168,  "Formating engine"
    30169,  "This property let you choose the pretty print and linearize formating engine. Currently, you have choice between:
- SimpleXml: A fast and low memory engine developped by LetMeSleepAlready (https://github.com/LetMeSleepAlready)
- QuickXml: A quick and simple engine which focus on conformity
- StringXml: An engine based on string processing. This engine is more permissive on invalid xml, but very slow on big xml files."
    30170,  "Auto-close tags"
    30171,  "Enable auto-close tags on pretty print. For instance, when enabled, ""<sample></sample>"" is replaced with ""<sample/>""."
    30172,  "Ensure conformity"
    30173,  "Make the prettyprint/linearize engine maintain XML conformity. Whitespace are trimmed and linebreaks are added only if it does not modify the xml structure. Currently only available on QuickXml."
    30174,  "Max indent level"
    30175,  "The max indentation level for pretty print. A zero (0) value means no indentation limit"
END

